+//
+// S202 WAVE-2 REBUILD of the wave-1 host-native artifact
+// tools/native_host/libgdx-freetype64.so (lost to the sandbox recycle —
+// the wave-1 report's [GDX-HOST] LOADED REAL row requires exactly this
+// file). Built AGAINST HOST FREETYPE 2.13.3 (the sqlite law: load a REAL
+// library, never fabricate). The APK's own bionic libgdx-freetype.so is
+// x86_64 and dlopens, but its FT tail answered garbage (the S200 noise
+// face) — the wrapper gives the engine REAL glyph memory on the host.
+//
+// Contract (from androguard manifest FT_NATIVE_MANIFEST.json, tictactoe
+// classes.dex: 68 natives / 72 call sites, all J-handle based):
+//   every native receives (JNIEnv*, thiz, jlong handle, ...) per the
+//   engine's call_native (slot 0 = env, slot 1 = receiver). The wrapper
+//   uses ONLY engine-implemented env slots: 229 NewDirectByteBuffer,
+//   230 GetDirectBufferAddress, 231 GetDirectBufferCapacity (the
+//   F-NEW-590 family). JNI mangling: $ -> _00024 (F-NEW-611 law).
+//
+// Honest-pointer law: handles are REAL FT pointers; owned FT_Glyph
+// objects (FT_Get_Glyph / FT_Glyph_To_Bitmap / FT_Glyph_StrokeBorder
+// results) are registry-tracked so Glyph.done never destroys a
+// face-owned slot glyph. Silence by default: MINIANDROID_FT_WRAP_TRACE=1
+// emits one bounded row per call (determinism-neutral when unset).
